=======================================================================================================
FRAME GEOMETRY SURVEY + PROBE CALIBRATION  -  21/08/2026
=======================================================================================================
Session record. Covers Z probe trigger height, the P5/P9 resolution, a bed.g
motor-order bug, and a full gantry geometry survey cross-checked against a
Mitutoyo DTI. Ends with a shim schedule and an order list.

Machine state during all of this: damaged/temporary granite slab fitted, no bed
heater attached, hotend PT1000 still failed (so everything COLD). Replacement
slab on order.

-------------------------------------------------------------------------------
1. HEADLINE FINDINGS
-------------------------------------------------------------------------------
*** READ THIS FIRST: three heightmaps were taken. ONLY RUN 3 IS VALID. ***
    run 1 (16:21) - taken with LOOSE HOTEND SCREWS and the buggy bed.g motor
                    ordering. Overstated the rear tilt by ~2x. DISCARD.
    run 2 (18:46) - screws tight, but the centre G30 failed silently so the
                    datum was unset. SHAPE is valid, absolute datum is not.
    run 3 (18:57) - tight, correct ordering, datum verified. THE REFERENCE.
    run3 vs run2 agree to rms 0.0043mm / worst 0.012mm across 49 points.
    run3 vs run1 differ by rms 0.0454mm / worst 0.136mm.

a) The right Y rail sits LOW at the rear by 0.203mm across the 380mm probe span
   (0.294mm at the actual 550mm rail centres). Front rails level to 0.024mm.
   Cause: assembly geometry, not a loose joint - see section 5.

b) Both Y rails bow upward mid-span by ~0.2mm (left +0.196, right +0.225).
   COMMON MODE, so no beam roll. Leave it - mesh cancels it exactly.
   This figure reproduced across all three runs including the bad one.

c) The X beam is good: 0.100mm bow over 380mm = 0.26 mm/m. Do not touch it.

d) THE MACHINE IS REPEATABLE to 0.0043mm rms between independent cold runs,
   once the toolhead is tight. The frame is not moving.

e) G31 trigger height -0.030 +/-0.005, slip gauge, tight assembly. Still COLD;
   redo hot when the PT1000 lands. See section 3.

f) M92 Z800 is CORRECT, verified by calipers against physical bed travel.

